STEP 12 — Tests: unit, integration and Selenium (end-to-end)

The project now has four kinds of automated tests:

    layer        where                       what it checks                                       how many
    -----------  --------------------------  ---------------------------------------------------  --------
    unit (BE)    test/unit/                  single Python functions: password hashing, JWT,          35
                                             input validation, role check, CORS setting
    unit (FE)    frontend/src/**/*.test.js   single JS functions: date format, error messages,         9
                                             role maps (Vitest)
    integration  test/integration/           the real FastAPI app + real MySQL test database:         43
                                             login, refresh, logout, /auth/me, roles, admin users
    e2e          test/e2e/                   Selenium drives a real Edge browser through the          35
                                             real frontend + backend: every page and flow

None of them touch the real `inspektorati` database: they use
`inspektorati_test`, which is dropped, recreated and migrated (Alembic) at
the start of every pytest run.

-------------------------------------------------------------------------
HOW TO RUN  (Windows PowerShell, from the project root inspektorati-ai\)
-------------------------------------------------------------------------
All backend tests at once (unit + integration + Selenium, about 4 minutes):
    backend\venv\Scripts\python.exe -m pytest

One layer at a time:
    backend\venv\Scripts\python.exe -m pytest test\unit           (seconds)
    backend\venv\Scripts\python.exe -m pytest test\integration    (about 35 s)
    backend\venv\Scripts\python.exe -m pytest test\e2e            (about 3 min)
or by marker:
    backend\venv\Scripts\python.exe -m pytest -m unit
    backend\venv\Scripts\python.exe -m pytest -m "not e2e"        (everything except Selenium)

Useful options:
    -v                 show every test name
    -x                 stop at the first failure
    -k login           run only tests whose name contains "login"

Frontend unit tests (from inside frontend\):
    npm test

-------------------------------------------------------------------------
SELENIUM (test/e2e) — what you need to know
-------------------------------------------------------------------------
- Requirements: MySQL running, Microsoft Edge installed, Node/npm installed.
  The first run needs internet once: Selenium downloads the matching
  Edge driver by itself (Selenium Manager) and caches it.
- You do NOT need to start the servers yourself. The tests start their own:
      backend   http://localhost:8001   (database inspektorati_test)
      frontend  http://localhost:5180   (talks to the backend on 8001)
  and stop them at the end. Ports 8001 and 5180 must be free; your normal
  dev servers (8000 / 5173 / 5174) can keep running.
- The seed users (admin / inspektor / drejtor) are created in the test
  database automatically.
- Watch the browser while the tests run:
      $env:E2E_HEADED = "1"; backend\venv\Scripts\python.exe -m pytest test\e2e
  Use Chrome instead of Edge:
      $env:E2E_BROWSER = "chrome"
  (remove them again with:  Remove-Item Env:E2E_HEADED, Env:E2E_BROWSER)

What the Selenium tests cover:
- Landing: headline, both paths, AI highlight, admin note, stema logo,
  no "create account" link; citizen button -> /kerkese; staff buttons
  (header and hero) -> /kycu.
- Login page: texts, logo, back link; empty fields error; wrong password and
  unknown email error; show/hide password; login with the Enter key.
- /regjistrohu and unknown pages go back to the landing page.
- Logged out: /inspektor, /drejtor, /admin, /admin/perdoruesit -> /kycu.
- Each role (inspektor, drejtor, admin): lands on its own dashboard, sees
  "Mirë se erdhe, {emri}! Roli juaj është {roli}.", its protected API route
  answers (LEJUAR), name and role in the sidebar.
- Wrong role is sent to its own dashboard; logged-in user opening /kycu is
  sent to the dashboard; only the admin sees "Përdoruesit & rolet".
- Welcome message can be closed and shows only once; the session survives a
  page reload; logout clears the session and closes the protected pages.
- Admin: dashboard link to user management; creates a user who can then log
  in; duplicate email error; edits a user; deactivates a user (confirm
  dialog) who is then locked out, reactivates them and they can log in
  again; no "Çaktivizo" button on their own row; "Anulo" closes the form.

